# Changes from draft-melnikov-email-big-files-00 {#changes}
{:numbered="false"}

* Renamed the header field from "Content-External" to
  "Link-Attachment", and changed its syntax from that of Content-Type
  to that of Content-Disposition.

* Moved the header field from the header section of the fallback body
  part to the message header section.

* Added the "cid" parameter, and the HTML markup that uses it.

* Added the "key" parameter, which names an encrypting HTTP content
  coding and gives the key, for encrypted files.  The same format is
  used in download links.

* Made "size" and "digest-sha-256" required, and took digest algorithm
  names from the HTTP Digest Fields registry.

* Renamed "name" to "filename", to match Content-Disposition, and
  replaced the media type with the optional "type" parameter.

* Removed the "permission" parameter: a linked attachment can't
  change, like an attached file.

* Added requirements for attachment servers, receiving servers and
  message stores: unguessable URLs, fetching during scanning, local
  storage with access by digest, and lifetime tied to the message.

* Wrote the Security and Privacy Considerations.

